:"1795153883174778001-f6acceeb-e6e8-404e-a821-b641df37e183"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"72629257a719e00a8befe79891c696de7363d5b5ed4187e549ee0b23c53da84c","event_uuid":"c3fb979d-d518-4dee-9102-9cb662811f97","position":{"commit_sha":"57b6036c1d4163449445ec55407e78be677dd041","position":"1795153895658453001-c3fb979d-d518-4dee-9102-9cb662811f97"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"f67f184c6091b241911cabb4126dc93e8be00da8ba375149b10966988b50bf91","event_uuid":"86742fb8-6b3b-4d9f-80da-c8df87a15661","position":{"commit_sha":"73342190a4f1185aff447548c1aa2e75e7d3e9d8","position":"1795184450884817001-86742fb8-6b3b-4d9f-80da-c8df87a15661"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Enumeration of product readers of files published through atomic_write / replace_with_retry / os.replace (origin/main 717c50f8b33, 2026-11-19 PST). This records acceptance criterion 1; the exposed-and-fixed list is in the description.\n\nEvery product reader of a file published by `atomic_write`/`replace_with_retry`/`os.replace` in `src/rebar` was traced. No read-side retry exists in the tree: the only `PermissionError` handling around a publish is the writer's `replace_with_retry` (`src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:45-65`).\n\nNot exposed: event files, new SNAPSHOT names (`_commands/txn.py`, `_store/staging.py`, `compact_txn.py`, `compact_rebuild.py`), whose destination never exists before the rename.\n\nLock-protected (reader and writer hold the same lock): `hlc.state` (`_store/hlc.py:78`), `bytes.total` read-modify-write inside `add_bytes` (`_snapshot/cache.py:104`), `.store-compat.json` read-modify-write (`compat.py:437`, `project_ensures.py:111`, under `ensures.py:157`), the compaction intent journal (`compact_recovery.py:132`), the recent-creates journal (`recent_creates.py:146`), `projects.json` inside the locked set/remove (`projects_store.py:209`), the snapshot integrity digest under the GC interlock (`janitor.py:267`), and `mapping.json` under `mutate_json_object`'s sibling lock (`sidecar_transactions.py:61`).\n\nExposed but needing no change, because a refused read is a cheap cache miss that is recomputed and rewritten: `.opcert-key.pub` (`_opcert_signing.py:222`), the reducer cache (`reducer/_cache.py:37`), the graph cache (`graph/_cache.py:61`), snapshot caveats (`_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:164`), the review-bot cursor (`review_bot/reconcile.py:94`).","timestamp":1795152726167867001},{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change committed in worktree w05-willet (7f648092f6f): retry_contended/open_published/published_is_file plus 39 reader edits in 28 modules; tests/unit/store/test_fsutil_read_retry.py (44 tests) passes. The first make verify ran inside a command sandbox that blocks ssh-agent and network (51 failures, including test_reclaim_resign: 9 fail sandboxed, 8 of 9 pass unsandboxed); it is not valid evidence and will be rerun outside the sandbox.","timestamp":1795184450884817001}],"created_at":1795066565486207587,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"fddbe6bf-38ad-4a34-b884-5aee4e75e907","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f59a-4c53-9452-4d3f"}],"description":"## Observation\nIn Windows sweep run 44456347985 (job 135332660982, main at ab323f7df0c), `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_bridge_state_atomic_write_concurrency.py::test_peer_confirmations_distinct_concurrent_saves_are_merged` failed with `PermissionError(13, 'Permission denied')` recorded by the test's concurrent READER thread (`final_path.read_text()`, `:43-47`), not by the writers. The writers now retry a contended replace (`rebar._store.fsutil.replace_with_retry`, sporting-feudalist-bluet). On Windows, opening a file while `MoveFileEx(MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING)` replaces it can fail with access denied; POSIX readers never see this.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n- Product readers that open a published sidecar, cache or cursor without holding the writer's lock (for example a store's initial load) can get the same transient `PermissionError` on Windows and treat it as a failed or empty read.\n- Readers that already read under the sibling lock (`sidecar_transactions.mutate_json_object`) are unaffected.\n\n## Enumeration\nThe full enumeration (not exposed, lock-protected, exposed-but-harmless cache misses) is recorded in this ticket's comment of 2026-11-19. No read-side retry exists in the tree; the only `PermissionError` handling around a publish is the writer's `replace_with_retry` (`src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:45-65`).\n\nExposed with a harmful outcome (crash, a silent wrong default, or a lost write), all fixed here:\n- Crash / fail-closed: `_store/compat.py:341` (`_analyze`, reached from `lock.acquire` at `_store/lock.py:373`, so every write command fails while an ensure republishes the record) and `:164` (`_local_store_epoch`); `_config_sources.py:120,128` (`rebar.toml` stat and open; also reached by `_config_writer.py:221`); `_cli/__init__.py:174`; `llm/evals/eval.py:80`; `llm/evals/provider_parity.py:221`; `reconciler/projects_store.py:69`; `reconciler/binding_repository.py:262`; `_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:68-71`; `llm/workflow/completion_banking.py:543`.\n- Lost or wrong write: `_commands/session_log.py:55` (an unreadable pointer starts a new session log and overwrites the pointer); `_commands/bridge_repair.py:68` (an empty retired set disables Guard 2 before `save()`); `_snapshot/cache.py:92` (`byte_total` read as 0 makes `janitor.py:314-315` add the full total again); `reconciler/get_rotation.py:30`; `llm/gate_runs.py:179` (a terminal record read as absent can be overwritten by `_materialize_stale_running`, `:389-403`).\n- Silent wrong default: `llm/prompting/prompts.py:190,351,522` (a user prompt override silently replaced by the packaged prompt); `_commands/identity.py:38` (events stamped without the current identity); `_store/push_state.py:143` (PUSH_PENDING hidden); `_store/ensures.py:113,207`; `_commands/scratch.py:158`; `_ids.py:119`; `_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py:21`; `reconciler/alert_store.py:63,123`; `reconciler/last_pass.py:183`; `reconciler/binding_repository.py:196,284`; `reconciler/peer_confirmations.py:71`; `reconciler/impossible_links.py:195`; `llm/plan_review/checkpoints.py:117` and `llm/workflow/completion_verdict_cache.py:258` (a refused read reruns a billable LLM call).\n\n## Approach\nMove the contended-path retry loop out of `replace_with_retry` into one helper, `fsutil.retry_contended(fn, *args, **kwargs)`: on Windows it retries `PermissionError` with the existing backoff and 2 s deadline (`_REPLACE_RETRY_DEADLINE_S`), then re-raises; elsewhere it calls `fn` once. `replace_with_retry` becomes `retry_contended(os.replace, src, dst)`, unchanged in behaviour. Add `fsutil.open_published(path, mode=\"r\", *, encoding=\"utf-8\")`, which is `retry_contended(open, ...)` (encoding omitted for binary modes); the refusal happens when the file is opened, so retrying the open is enough. Each exposed reader above replaces its `open(...)`/`Path.read_text(...)` with `open_published(...)` (and `_config_sources.py:120` wraps its `path.stat()` in `retry_contended`), keeping its existing exception handling, so a refusal that outlasts the deadline still takes the same path as today. A refused replace also refuses a stat, so an existence check before the open is exposed in the same way: `Path.exists()`/`is_file()` re-raise `PermissionError` on Python 3.11/3.12 and return False on 3.13+, and `os.path.exists`/`isfile` return False. Where a listed reader checks existence of the file it then opens (`binding_repository.py:193,260,281`, `projects_store.py:66`, `prompts.py:189,350`, `scratch.py:154`, `checkpoints.py:116`, `eval.py:77`, `bridge_repair.py:65`, and any other such check in a listed reader), the check is removed and `FileNotFoundError` raised by `open_published` maps to the reader's existing absent branch. Absence is then decided only by an open, and only `PermissionError` is retried. Existence checks that gate a read but sit outside a reader function use a third helper, `fsutil.published_is_file(path)`: `stat.S_ISREG(retry_contended(os.stat, path).st_mode)`, mapping `FileNotFoundError`/`NotADirectoryError` to False. It replaces `is_file()` on published config files in `_config_sources._discover_project_config` (`rt.is_file()` `:175` for `rebar.toml`, `pp.is_file()` `:184` for `pyproject.toml`) and `raw_layers` (`up.is_file()` `:209`, the user config), and `os.path.exists` on `.store-compat.json` in `_store/store_usability._carries_store_structure` (`:55`). Without it, a refused stat on Python 3.13+ makes discovery silently skip the project `rebar.toml` while `_config_writer.py:221` republishes it. POSIX behaviour is unchanged: on POSIX both helpers are a single direct call. Reusing the existing Windows switch `_RETRY_CONTENDED_REPLACE` adds no config key, environment variable or flag.\n\nThe unlocked read-modify-write in `alert_store.patch_bug_filed` (`alert_store.py:118-147`) can also drop an append made between its read and its replace, on every platform. That is a separate race, not this Windows read refusal; it is filed as equable-overseas-hoiho.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py` (`retry_contended`, `open_published`, `published_is_file`; `replace_with_retry` delegates)\n- `src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py` (`_carries_store_structure`)\n- The reader modules listed under \"Exposed with a harmful outcome\" (one call-site swap each)\n- `tests/unit/store/test_fsutil_read_retry.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n- New unit tests force the Windows branch (`monkeypatch.setattr(fsutil, \"_RETRY_CONTENDED_REPLACE\", True)`) and inject an `open` that raises `PermissionError` twice and then succeeds: `open_published` returns the content; a refusal that outlasts a shortened deadline re-raises `PermissionError`; `FileNotFoundError` propagates at once. On the POSIX branch one `PermissionError` propagates immediately.\n- A wiring test parses each fixed reader module and asserts each listed reader function (including `_discover_project_config`, `raw_layers` and `_carries_store_structure`) calls `open_published`, `retry_contended` or `published_is_file` and makes no `exists()`/`is_file()`/`os.path.exists`/`os.path.isfile` call, so the enumeration cannot silently regress.\n- For each reader whose existence guard is removed, its existing absent-file test (or a new one in the new test module) still gets the absent default when the file does not exist.\n- Existing `replace_with_retry` tests keep passing; `make verify` passes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The product read paths of files published through `atomic_write`/`replace_with_retry` are enumerated, and each is recorded as either lock-protected or exposed on Windows.\n- [ ] Every exposed read path tolerates the transient refusal (or is shown not to need to), with a Windows-branch unit test.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py","reason":"retry_contended and open_published helpers"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/store_usability.py","reason":"retried existence check on .store-compat.json"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sources.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/projects_store.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/binding_repository.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/session_log.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/bridge_repair.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/cache.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/get_rotation.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/identity.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push_state.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/scratch.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_ids.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/alert_store.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/last_pass.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/peer_confirmations.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/impossible_links.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/checkpoints.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_verdict_cache.py","reason":"route the exposed read of an atomically published file through open_published"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_fsutil_read_retry.py","reason":"Windows-branch retry and reader wiring tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f6acceeb-e6e8-404e-a821-b641df37e183","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"2781-42c5-201c-4efe","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows: readers of an atomically replaced file can get PermissionError while a replace is in flight","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8322bd6b-35d2-4a8a-8a94-d3ab02797de0","145b9474-5364-4985-97da-05d18d9d8631","8fa236ca-6480-449f-b8de-1b58b31220f2","ca41c929-2c70-4269-809e-ac6f150d7ce4","2a09c0b5-8a63-496d-8821-4f77111473e0","496ae474-50eb-41f1-a7cf-62f81f942cdb","35d4b920-abda-42ef-a4a4-cf81d47e5943","dc9207e0-fdab-4627-8f55-88e809463b69","f6acceeb-e6e8-404e-a821-b641df37e183","c3fb979d-d518-4dee-9102-9cb662811f97","86742fb8-6b3b-4d9f-80da-c8df87a15661"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795184450884817002,"uuid":"a93b62f4-4477-4980-a5dc-029fe899e0a8"}
